### PR Title
Add CloudWatch Alarm for Missing Jenkins Controller Logs

### Summary
This PR introduces CloudWatch monitoring to detect when Jenkins controller heartbeat logs stop streaming to AWS CloudWatch. The implementation provides automated alerting through the existing Jenkins SNS notification infrastructure to improve visibility into CloudWatch log delivery failures.

### Changes Made
- Updated the CloudWatch Agent configuration to collect Jenkins heartbeat logs alongside existing Jenkins build logs.
- Updated the Jenkins controller user-data script to generate heartbeat events every minute using cron.
- Added a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to track incoming Jenkins heartbeat events.
- Added a CloudWatch alarm that triggers when heartbeat events are missing for five consecutive minutes.
- Configured alarm and recovery notifications through the existing Jenkins SNS topic.
- Retained existing Jenkins ASG capacity and EFS storage monitoring configurations.
- Corrected the Terraform metric filter argument from `filter_pattern` to `pattern`.

### Validation
- Run `terraform fmt -recursive` to verify Terraform formatting.
- Run `terraform validate` to confirm configuration validity.
- Review `terraform plan` for expected infrastructure changes.
- Verify Jenkins heartbeat events are received in CloudWatch.
- Simulate a log delivery failure by stopping the CloudWatch Agent container.
- Confirm the CloudWatch alarm transitions to ALARM and sends an SNS notification.
- Restart the CloudWatch Agent container and verify the alarm returns to OK.

### Expected Outcome
The monitoring system detects missing Jenkins heartbeat logs within approximately five minutes and notifies the team through the existing SNS alerting mechanism, reducing the risk of unnoticed CloudWatch log delivery interruptions.

### Backout Plan
Revert the CloudWatch heartbeat metric filter and alarm resources through Terraform. Remove the heartbeat cron configuration and restore the previous CloudWatch Agent configuration if necessary.
